---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Metabolic Intelligence · Klere"
  description="Klere positioning: energy is the binding constraint. Metabolic Intelligence at the edge and a resource-optimized central datacenter. Hyperscale water and power are not required by design. Research owns the class. Klere owns the product. board_synth_claimed=false."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Paper 4 · about · one-pager</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Metabolic Intelligence for Klere
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Why this is the future.</strong> Energy is the binding constraint (Shannon, Landauer, Value of Information).
      The transformer corridor can keep improving and still plateau as a deployment future, because uncapped import is no longer what buys the next useful answer.
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Metabolic Intelligence</strong> is the class that takes a budget in and returns the best answer that budget can buy.
      It is designed for <strong class="text-brand-white">Klere</strong> (<a href="https://klere.ai" class="text-brand-cyan">klere.ai</a>).
      Research owns the class. Klere owns the product.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Where it runs.</strong> The <strong class="text-brand-white">edge</strong>
      (coin-cell tags, digital enzymes, metabolic schedules) and the
      <strong class="text-brand-white">resource-optimized central</strong> datacenter
      (budget-capped, grid-following lean campus under OpenADR / DSX Flex).
      Not an uncapped transformer hyperscale campus.
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Mixture of Limits</strong> chooses the gear: Lookup, then Formula, then Solver, then Model last.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">What a skeptic has to deny.</strong>
      People should not have to fight over energy to eat or to use AI.
      At these envelopes, dedicated water plants, dedicated power plants, and hyperscale cooling loops are
      <strong class="text-brand-white">not required by design</strong>
      (design consequence of microwatt-class tags and the lean-campus pack, not invented liters saved).
      Dismissals and their evidence class are in the paper's objection ledger.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 glass-card p-6 space-y-3" id="investor-one-pager">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Investor / partner one-pager</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Problem.</strong> The default future is transformer scale plus the hyperscale power and water plant that scale presupposes.
        Cold-chain and grid operators need intelligence that fits a stated joule envelope. Energy binds. Uncapped import does not.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Offer.</strong> Klere embodies Metabolic Intelligence as edge and lean central under an explicit budget.
        Digital enzymes recognize under MCU budgets. A metabolic grid service pulls ordered levers when the grid asks the plant to cut.
        The <code class="text-brand-cyan">J(m|q)</code> obtain-router prices Lookup → Formula → Solver → Model LAST under stake λ.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Why not hyperscale water/power.</strong>
        The class targets lower continuous budgets by construction (µW tags; MW-capped lean campus).
        Hyperscale support plants are outside the design. Sell that as a design consequence with pack evidence.
        Do not invent gallons saved or board <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Evidence classes (sell separately).</strong>
        <em>Proven pack:</em> emulator enzyme vs MLP counts; SmellNet sequential protocol; datasheet+schedule ~10 µW tag model;
        OpenADR 3.1 / DSX Flex protocol demos + scenario table; obtain-router math / ledger bands.
        <em>Roadmap:</em> Klere SKU packaging for tags, lean-campus operator product, gateway DX beyond soft-ref companions.
        <em>Estimate:</em> Wh/answer curves, CR2032 years, campus plant watts. Labeled until Metered.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">GTM slices.</strong>
        (1) Edge pack: recognition and schedule evidence. Roadmap SKU.
        (2) Lean-campus flexibility: protocol demos and scenario table. Roadmap operator product.
        (3) Obtain stack: router math and soft-ref companions. Roadmap gateway packaging.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Peer honesty.</strong>
        Logical Intelligence, World Labs / V-JEPA, Dynamo / DSX / AEMA, and neuromorphic MCUs own slices.
        None presently combine tag ↔ lean-campus + OpenADR/DSX + <code class="text-brand-cyan">J(m|q)</code> + enzymes as one class.
        Soft-ref: <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Forbidden without meters.</strong>
        Invented liters/gallons saved; Wh/answer as board <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>;
        AEMA latency numbers; Anwar chicken accuracy; “100% served through 90% cut” as a universal field claim.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion laws</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Catalog triad stays intact:
        <a href="/papers/mol/" class="text-brand-cyan">Navigation</a> (Mixture of Limits) ·
        <a href="/papers/ni/" class="text-brand-cyan">Commit</a> (Notational Intelligence) ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Economic Reality of Satiation</a>.
        Fourth study: <strong class="text-brand-white">Energy budget / Metabolic Intelligence</strong> (this study).
        See <a href="/#companion-laws" class="text-brand-cyan">catalog triad</a> and
        <a href="/#metabolic-intelligence" class="text-brand-cyan">energy-budget strip</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/mei/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/mei.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Teaching figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Paths</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/papers/mei/</span> → study prose (glossary + claim ledger in appendices)</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/pdfs/mei.pdf</span> → downloadable study PDF</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/living/mei/</span> → teaching figures (Manim + pack charts)</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/about/mei/</span> → this Klere positioning one-pager</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Status and measurement bounds</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Research study, not a journal final. Public klere.ai is thin access framing, not a shipped feature catalog.
        Datasheet + schedule ≠ board package power. Emulator instruction counts ≠ wattmeter.
        Curves / ledger Wh are labeled estimates or measured-kernel models.
        Soft-ref path: <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code> only when Metered;
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
